  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "Rated for aquariums up to about 600 litres.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 300 W built-in heater removes the need for an in-tank heater, which keeps the tank looking cleaner.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "For tanks up to 250 L or 350 L, the smaller 250/350 models in the range are the better match; the 850 handles tanks up to about 800 L.",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "In one test, real flow at 80 cm head was only about 456 L/h, so a large or heavily stocked tank may need extra circulation.",
      "source": 4
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "Before switching on, fill the pre-filter chamber with water (or open the lid and fill the canister) to prime it.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Unplug the unit before installing or servicing it.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The EasyClean pre-filter comes off separately, so you can rinse it often without opening the main canister, which helps the main media last longer.",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "It comes with filter wool and basic media, which you can swap for other media.",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "Handle safety locks and check valves on the connections help prevent leaks when you disconnect it; flow can be adjusted at several points.",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "A reviewer found it easy to start up and maintain.",
      "source": 4
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "Several owners report the 600 sucking air (possibly through the heater's top seal or O-ring), which causes bubbles in the tank and impeller noise; users said the 250/350 sizes didn't have this problem.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "Noise varies from unit to unit: some owners report a bassy hum, while others find it quiet. OASE reportedly updated the unit after complaints.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "Some users say it is hard to prime and the flow feels weak.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "In a bench test it drew about 15.7 W instead of the stated 22 W and was very quiet, but measured flow was far below the 1250 L/h rating.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "A blog review measured about 32–36 dB at 1 m.",
      "source": 6
    },
    {
      "fact": "Vietnamese listings often mix up the plain BioMaster 600 and the Thermo version with a heater; confirm the heater is included before you buy.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Vietnamese sellers don't cover removable parts under warranty.",
      "source": 1
    }
  ],
